      "text": "The center is the midpoint of the line segment connecting the points $(0,4)$ and $(1,3)$. The midpoint is at $(1/2,7/2)$, which lies on the $x$-axis. The coordinates of the center are $(a,0)$. Using the distance formula, the distance between the center and either of the points is its radius. Squaring the distance and subtracting twice the radius and $a$ from it gives a quadratic equation whose solutions are the square of the radius and $a$. Simplifying and factoring this quadratic up to $(s-a)k^2$, we find that $a$ is the sum of two distinct primes. Therefore, the radius of the circle is $\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{2}}$.",
